  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "When I {was} a little girl, I liked drawing, {freely} and {joyously} making marks on {the} walls at home.In {primary} {school} , I learned to write using {chalk} .Writing seemed to be another form of {drawing} .I shaped individual letters {into} repeating lines, {which} were {abstract} forms, {delightful} but {meaningless} {patterns} .",
      "cn": "当我还 <u> 是 </u> 个小女孩的时候，我就喜欢画画，在家里的墙壁上 <u> 自由 </u> 、 <u> 愉快地 </u> 涂涂画画。上 <u> 小学 </u> 时，我学会了用 <u> 粉笔 </u> 写字。写字似乎是另一种形式的 <u> 绘画 </u> 。我把单个字母塑造 <u> 成 </u> 重复的线条， <u> 这些线条 </u> 具有 <u> 抽象的 </u> 形式，是 <u> 令人愉悦 </u> 却 <u> 没有意义的图案 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "In {secondary} school, art was {my} favorite subject.Since I loved {it} so much I thought I was good at it. {For} the art O-level {exam} I had to present an {oil} {painting} .I found it difficult, but still {hoped} to {pass} .I failed, with a low grade.I'd been {over-confident} . {Now} I'd been {declared} {talentless} .",
      "cn": "<u> 中学 </u> 时，美术是 <u> 我 </u> 最喜欢的科目。因为我非常喜欢 <u> 它 </u> ，所以我以为自己擅长于此。在美术的普通学科水平 <u> 考试中 </u> ，我需要提交一幅 <u> 油画 </u> 。我觉得这很难，但仍然 <u> 希望 </u> 能考试 <u> 及格 </u> 。结果我没及格，分数很低。我之前 <u> 太过自信 </u> 了。 <u> 现在 </u> 我被 <u> 判定 </u> 为 <u> 没有天赋 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "But {channels} {of} creativity {stayed} open {elsewhere} : I {went} on writing poems and stories.Still, I went to {exhibitions} often.I continued my {habitual} drawing, which I now {characterized} {as} {childish} doodling ( (乱画) ).In my 30s, I made {painter} friends {and} learned new ways of looking at art.However, I couldn't {let} myself have a go at actually doing it.Though these new friends were abstract painters using oil {paints} , {or} were {printmakers} or {sculptors} , I took oil painting as the taboo ( (禁忌) ) high form I wasn't allowed to practice.",
      "cn": "但是，创造力 <u> 的渠道 </u> 在 <u> 别处 </u> 仍 <u> 保持 </u> 畅通：我 <u> 继续 </u> 写诗和故事。我依然经常去看 <u> 展览 </u> 。我保持着画画的 <u> 习惯 </u> ，但现在我把这 <u> 称为幼稚的 </u> 乱画。30多岁时，我结识了一些 <u> 画家 </u> 朋友， <u> 还 </u> 学会了以新的视角看待艺术。然而，我无法 <u> 让 </u> 自己真正去尝试做这件事。尽管这些新朋友都是使用油画 <u> 颜料 </u> 的抽象画家， <u> 或者 </u> 是 <u> 版画家 </u> 、 <u> 雕塑家 </u> ，但我把油画视为禁忌的高级艺术形式，认为自己不被允许进行尝试。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "{One} {night} , in my {early} 40s, I dreamed that a big woman in red {approached} {me} , handed me a bag of paints, and told me to start painting.The dream felt so authoritative that it shook me.It was a form of {energy} , {giving} me back something I'd lost. {Accordingly} , I started {by} experimenting with water colors. {Finally} , I {bought} some oil paints.",
      "cn": "在40岁 <u> 出头 </u> 的 <u> 一天夜里 </u> ，我梦见一个穿红衣服、身材高大的女人 <u> 走近我 </u> ，递给我一袋颜料，让我开始画画。这个梦充满威严，让我震撼不已。它是一种 <u> 能量 </u> ，将我曾经失去的某些东西重新还 <u> 给 </u> 了我。 <u> 于是 </u> ，我先 <u> 从 </u> 尝试水彩画开始。 <u> 最后 </u> ，我 <u> 买 </u> 了一些油画颜料。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "{Although} I have {enjoyed} breaking my decades-long taboo about working with oil paints, I have discovered I now prefer chalk and {ink} .I let my line drawings turn into {cartoons} I {send} to friends.It all feels free and easy.Un-anxious.This time around, I can accept my {limitations} but keep going.",
      "cn": "<u> 虽然 </u> 我很 <u> 享受 </u> 打破几十年来对使用油画颜料的禁忌，但是我发现自己现在更喜欢粉笔和 <u> 墨水 </u> 。我把线条画变成了 <u> 卡通画 </u> ， <u> 寄 </u> 给朋友们。这一切都让我感到轻松自由，没有焦虑。这一次，我可以接受自己的 <u> 局限 </u> ，但仍会继续坚持下去。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "Becoming a successful painter calls for being {resolute} .I realized I was always {afraid} of {wanting} {too} much.That dream {reminded} me that {those} {fears} and desires could encourage me to take {risks} and make experiments.",
      "cn": "成为一名成功的画家需要有 <u> 坚定的 </u> 决心。我意识到，我总是 <u> 害怕索求太 </u> 多。那个梦 <u> 提醒 </u> 我， <u> 那些恐惧 </u> 和欲望可以鼓励我去冒 <u> 险 </u> 和尝试。"
    }
  ],
